WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.240
Canadian police have broken up protests&nbsp;
against coronavirus restrictions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.440
which had been blocking an important trade&nbsp;
route with the US. A blockade of trucks and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.440
cars had stopped the flow of commerce&nbsp;
across the Ambassador Bridge - North&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.760
America's busiest border crossing. But&nbsp;
demonstrators at a larger protest are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.720
still occupying parts of the Canadian capital&nbsp;
Ottawa - to the annoyance of local residents.&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:31.680
Canada's busiest border crossing is getting ready&nbsp;
to re-open. After a week-long standoff at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:39.040
Ambassador Bridge, police in Windsor, Ontario,&nbsp;
have arrested dozens of protesters and cleared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:46.080
away vehicles that had blocked the vital highway.
Yeah, I`m frustrated that we're on day seven of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.560
this. I mean this, I could have told you from&nbsp;
the first hour that this is not going to end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.600
well unless we get in there and cut the head off&nbsp;
the snake very, very quickly. This is a crucial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:01.520
border crossing. We're talking about $400 million&nbsp;
a day that crosses at this one border crossing. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:07.440
the financial impact, you know, to now is nearing&nbsp;
$3 billion on our national economy. That's huge.&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.160
The situation in Canada's capital, Ottawa, remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:19.200
far from resolved. Trucks block the city center&nbsp;
and protesters camp out in front of Parliament.&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.200
Residents have had enough.
You're not free to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:29.200
anywhere you want in your city. I mean, there's&nbsp;
an illegal occupation happening. The rule of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:35.120
law doesn't exist a few blocks away. So&nbsp;
I mean, it's I guess it's intimidating.&nbsp;

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:41.360
Police have been reluctant to clear out protesters&nbsp;
as long as there are children with them.&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:48.640
Well, there's children here, and unfortunately,&nbsp;
parents are using their children, so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.840
I don't know. It's a really tough&nbsp;
situation for the police because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.720
you know, violence should not happen. So and,&nbsp;
I, the police are in a really tough situation.&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.880
Canada's Prime Minister Justin Trudeau&nbsp;
has told protesters it's time to go home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:18.560
They don't seem to be listening.

